[00:20.31] As he walks along the gorge's edge
[00:26.29] He meets a sense of yesteryear
[00:32.62] A window in the bank above his head
[00:38.68] Reveals his home amidst the streets
[00:45.55] Subway sounds, the sounds of complaint
[00:49.92] The smell of acid on his gun of paint
[00:54.91] As it carves out anger in a blood-red band
[01:00.02] Destroyed tomorrow by an unknown hand
[01:04.89] "My home!"
[01:08.24]
[01:10.27] Is this the way out from the endless scene
[01:15.95] Or just an entrance to another dream?
[01:20.04] And the light dies down on Broadway
[01:35.41] But as the skylight beckons him to leave
[01:41.95] He hears a scream from far below
[01:48.40] Within the raging water writhes the form
[01:54.68] Of brother John, he cries for help
[02:01.56] The gate is fading now, but open wide
[02:05.98] But John is drowning, I must decide
[02:10.95] Between the freedom I had in the rat-race
[02:16.08] Or to stay forever in this forsaken place
[02:20.92] "Hey John!"
[02:24.18]
[02:26.65] He makes for the river and the gate is gone
[02:31.76] Back to the void where it came from
[02:36.21] And the light dies down on Broadway
[02:49.14]